{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466438",
      "title": "Adding the Token to Outgoing Requests",
      "lectureOrder": 626,
      "videoOrder": 577,
      "sourceHash": "5b1213bea30141a814afcaf756b14dc2a5ba4a7e4285159b7d0bf8bea22bb485",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 5.13,
          "en": "Instructor: Why is our authentication status ignored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.13,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "when we try to fetch data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 11.85,
          "en": "Well, because just because we know that we are authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.85,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "and that we have the token somewhere in our user object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 17.85,
          "en": "Firebase doesn't know that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.85,
          "end": 20.43,
          "en": "We're not attaching it to that outgoing request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.43,
          "end": 22.92,
          "en": "and therefore Firebase has no chance of understanding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.92,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "that we have a valid token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 28.65,
          "en": "We need to add that token to the outgoing request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.65,
          "end": 31.56,
          "en": "to let Firebase know about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.56,
          "end": 34.02,
          "en": "And for that, we need to manipulate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.02,
          "end": 36.33,
          "en": "our outgoing HTDP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.33,
          "end": 38.94,
          "en": "that are related to data storing and fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "Hence, we need to look into the data storage service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "where we have fetch recipes and store recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 49.59,
          "en": "And these requests here now need to be edited such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.59,
          "end": 52.89,
          "en": "that we do attach our token to them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.89,
          "end": 53.987,
          "en": "the token we are storing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.987,
          "end": 56.673,
          "en": "in the user object in the auth service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.54,
          "end": 58.373,
          "en": "For that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.31,
          "end": 60.31,
          "en": "let's inject that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.173,
          "end": 63.6,
          "en": "auth service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.6,
          "end": 65.88,
          "en": "into the data storage service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.88,
          "end": 68.61,
          "en": "Of course, make sure you add the import path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.61,
          "end": 70.77,
          "en": "And now we need to get access to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 74.16,
          "en": "in both store recipes and fetch recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.16,
          "end": 76.23,
          "en": "because we need to get the token there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.23,
          "end": 78.53999999999999,
          "en": "Now we could set up a subscription to the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "but I don't care about every change to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.24,
          "en": "Instead, when we try to store or fetch recipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "I just want to get the token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 87.42,
          "en": "of the currently authenticated user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.42,
          "end": 89.733,
          "en": "I don't want to have an ongoing subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.57,
          "end": 93.06,
          "en": "Hence in the auth service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.06,
          "end": 96.84,
          "en": "we now should also store the token or the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.84,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "in a way that we can access it through different means.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 101.97,
          "en": "So not through a subject which is great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.97,
          "end": 104.88,
          "en": "for reactively updating the user interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.88,
          "end": 106.5,
          "en": "but that we also have a way of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.5,
          "end": 109.65,
          "en": "on demand fetching of the user data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 112.53,
          "en": "Now there are a couple of different ways of achieving that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.53,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "Since we're only interested in the token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 116.46000000000001,
          "en": "we could just store the token here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.46000000000001,
          "end": 117.34,
          "en": "in a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "which is null initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 122.43,
          "en": "and which will hold a string eventually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 122.43,
          "end": 125.46,
          "en": "where we set the token whenever we also emit a new subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 125.46,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "That would be possible and wouldn't be wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 131.31,
          "en": "but we can actually also use a different type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 131.31,
          "end": 132.87,
          "en": "of subject here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 135.84,
          "en": "This subject is a subject to which we can subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.84,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "and will get an information whenever new data is emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 143.22,
          "en": "Now actually there is a different type of subject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 143.22,
          "end": 146.463,
          "en": "RXJS offers, which is called behavior subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 149.73,
          "en": "Now this is also imported from RXJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 153.03,
          "en": "and generally it behaves just like the other subject,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 153.03,
          "end": 155.61,
          "en": "which means we can call next to emit a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 155.61,
          "end": 159.06,
          "en": "and we can subscribe to it to be informed about new values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.06,
          "end": 162.6,
          "en": "The difference is that behavior subject also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 166.65,
          "en": "gives subscribers immediate access to the previously",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 166.65,
          "end": 169.05,
          "en": "emitted value, even if they haven't subscribed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 169.05,
          "end": 172.02,
          "en": "at the point of time that value was emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 172.02,
          "end": 173.94,
          "en": "That means we can get access to the currently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.94,
          "end": 178.05,
          "en": "active user even if we only subscribe after",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.05,
          "end": 179.88,
          "en": "that user has been emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.88,
          "end": 181.38,
          "en": "So this means when we fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.38,
          "end": 183.78,
          "en": "and we need that token at this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 183.78,
          "end": 187.47,
          "en": "even if the user logged in before that point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 189.15,
          "en": "which will have been the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 189.15,
          "end": 191.67,
          "en": "we get access to that latest user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.67,
          "end": 194.58,
          "en": "Now the other behavior subject also needs to be initialized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.58,
          "end": 195.9,
          "en": "with a starting value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 195.9,
          "end": 197.64,
          "en": "which in my case will be null here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 197.64,
          "end": 199.07999999999998,
          "en": "It has to be a user object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 200.91,
          "en": "and null is a valid replacement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 204.03,
          "en": "because I don't wanna start off with a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 207.21,
          "en": "Now we don't need to change anything in the auth service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 207.21,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "We still emit our user as we do before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 211.89,
          "en": "with the next function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 211.89,
          "end": 214.74,
          "en": "But in our data storage service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 214.74,
          "end": 218.22,
          "en": "now we can reach out to the auth service user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 218.22,
          "end": 221.49,
          "en": "get the currently active user and be done with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 221.49,
          "end": 223.35,
          "en": "And that's just what I wanna do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 223.35,
          "end": 225.663,
          "en": "for example, when we fetch recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 226.5,
          "end": 229.86,
          "en": "So here we reach out to the auth service, there to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 229.86,
          "end": 231.69,
          "en": "And now the thing just is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 231.69,
          "end": 234.57,
          "en": "I don't wanna set up an ongoing subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 237.75,
          "en": "and still I need to subscribe to get that user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 237.75,
          "end": 240.21,
          "en": "So to make sure I only get the user once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 240.21,
          "end": 241.98,
          "en": "and thereafter I'm done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 241.98,
          "end": 244.47,
          "en": "of course we could manually immediately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 244.47,
          "end": 248.49,
          "en": "call unsubscribe thereafter, or you use pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 248.49,
          "end": 251.52,
          "en": "and then a special operator RXJS gives you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 251.52,
          "end": 254.61,
          "en": "and that would be the take operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 254.61,
          "end": 258.48,
          "en": "Take is also imported from RXJS operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 258.48,
          "end": 260.67,
          "en": "and take is called as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 263.01,
          "en": "and you simply pass a number to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 263.01,
          "end": 264.66,
          "en": "And I pass one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 264.66,
          "end": 266.43,
          "en": "And what this tells RXJS is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 266.43,
          "end": 270.87,
          "en": "that I only wanna take one value from that observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 270.87,
          "end": 274.05,
          "en": "and thereafter it should automatically unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 274.05,
          "end": 276.12,
          "en": "So this manages the subscription for me,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 276.12,
          "end": 278.4,
          "en": "gives me the latest user and unsubscribes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 278.4,
          "end": 281.31,
          "en": "and I'm not getting future users because I just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 281.31,
          "end": 284.49,
          "en": "want to get them on demand when fetch recipes is called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 284.49,
          "end": 285.9,
          "en": "So whenever this code executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 285.9,
          "end": 288.24,
          "en": "I don't wanna set up an ongoing subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 288.24,
          "end": 289.71,
          "en": "which gives me users at a point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 289.71,
          "end": 291.81,
          "en": "of time I don't need them anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 291.81,
          "end": 294.57,
          "en": "So thereafter here and subscribe, I get my user object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 294.57,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "but only once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 298.89,
          "en": "And we don't need to manually unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 298.89,
          "end": 301.56,
          "en": "In there we can then use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 301.56,
          "end": 302.393,
          "en": "this HTDP",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 303.3,
          "end": 306.27,
          "en": "request observable and set it up in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 306.27,
          "end": 309.27,
          "en": "and attach our token, which we get out of the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 309.27,
          "end": 312.78,
          "en": "The problem just is here we're in subscribe of an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 312.78,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "and here we create yet a number observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 315.15,
          "end": 317.7,
          "en": "And in the end I want to return this observable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 317.7,
          "end": 320.61,
          "en": "but returning from inside subscribe does not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 320.61,
          "end": 323.193,
          "en": "We have to return on the top level of this method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 324.21,
          "end": 327.9,
          "en": "The solution is that we pipe these two observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 327.9,
          "end": 330.81,
          "en": "the user observable and the HTDP observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 330.81,
          "end": 333.36,
          "en": "together into one big observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 333.36,
          "end": 335.82,
          "en": "And now this is getting a bit more advanced here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 335.82,
          "end": 337.40999999999997,
          "en": "related to RXJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 337.40999999999997,
          "end": 340.92,
          "en": "but still pretty easy to understand in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 340.92,
          "end": 344.19,
          "en": "You simply add another operator here to pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 344.19,
          "end": 345.96,
          "en": "for the user observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 345.96,
          "end": 350.15999999999997,
          "en": "And there we can use exhaust map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 350.15999999999997,
          "end": 353.97,
          "en": "Exhaust map is also imported from RXJS operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 353.97,
          "end": 355.77,
          "en": "And whilst the name might look strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 355.77,
          "end": 357.78,
          "en": "it does something very simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 357.78,
          "end": 360.09,
          "en": "It waits for the first observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 360.09,
          "end": 362.52,
